/* book exam traps: Counting only channel A gives one quarter of the available resolution and no direction at all — the examiner's favourite question. | Resolution is not accuracy: the slot pitch sets resolution, but disc eccentricity, mounting tilt and bearing play set the true accuracy. | Raw Gray code is not a number. Reading a Gray word as if it were binary gives a wrong position; convert Gray to binary by XOR first. | Unit slip on linear scales: a 20 µm pitch with ×4 gives 5 µm per count, not 20 µm. Divide, do not stop at the pitch. | An incremental encoder loses its count when power fails; on restart the axis must be homed on the Z pulse before any position reading is trusted. */
