/* book: lead: Speed is everywhere on a plant floor: motor shafts, turbine rotors, paper rolls. Three cheap ways turn speed into an electrical reading. A tachogenerator is a small generator whose voltage rises with speed. A stroboscope flashes light at a known rate and freezes the shaft for the eye. Variable-frequency sensors carry the measurement in a signal's frequency, read by a counter or a frequency-to-volt */
