/* book Worked example 2: Q: A pick-up on a 60-tooth gear feeds 200 µs pulses of height 5 V to an RC averaging filter. The output is 0.25 V. Find the pulse frequency and the shaft speed in rpm.
   1. fin = Vout / (Vref T) = 0.25 / (5 × 200 × 10⁻⁶) = 250 Hz.
   2. One pulse per tooth, so the shaft makes fin/z turns per second: n = 60 fin / z = 60 × 250 / 60 = 250 rpm, with z = 60 teeth.
   Answer: The pulse frequency is 250 Hz and the shaft turns at 250 rpm. */
