/* book: lead: A force-balance transducer does not read how far a spring bends. It detects a tiny beam motion and drives a coil current until the coil's magnetic force cancels the input force. The coil current then measures force or pressure. This closed loop gives high accuracy and a current output that survives long cables. It appears in pressure transmitters, precision weighing and servo accelerometers. */
/* book Figure 4.9.1: The diaphragm pushes the beam up with 2 N; the gap sensor sees the first micrometres of motion, and the amplifier drives the coil until B I L also equals 2 N. The balance current of 0.16 A is the measurement, sent on as 16.8 mA. */
