/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - An input force pushes a balance beam.
   - F is force in newtons (N); B is gap flux density in tesla (T); I is coil current in amperes (A); L is total conductor length in the coil in metres (m).
   - The beam moves only micrometres, so spring creep and hysteresis hardly affect the reading.
   - Closed-loop sensitivity is 1/(B L) amperes per newton.
   - High loop gain keeps the error small.
   - A stable magnet and a stiff coil former matter; temperature changes in the magnet shift the span.
   - A pressure transmitter uses a diaphragm to turn pressure into force on the beam.
*/
